() Tj
T*
(   3. Step-by-Step Procedure for FBD Construction:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1 [System Identification]: Clearly choose and outline the structural boundary of the body.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2 [Isolation]: Sketch the geometric profile of the body detached from physical supports.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3 [Active Loads]: Draw all known applied loads, indicating exact points of application,) Tj
T*
(   lines of action, and sense of direction with clear numerical magnitudes.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4 [Support Constraints]: Replace physical supports with equivalent reaction vectors:) Tj
T*
(   - Smooth roller / rocker: 1 reaction force perpendicular to supporting plane.) Tj
T*
(   - Hinge / pin connection: 2 mutually orthogonal reaction forces \(Rx, Ry\).) Tj
T*
(   - Fixed / encastre wall: 2 reaction forces \(Rx, Ry\) and 1 reactive restraint couple \(M\).) Tj
T*
(   - Flexible cable: 1 tensile force directed along the cable axis away from the body.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5 [Coordinate Reference & Dimensions]: Establish Cartesian axes \(+x horizontal, +y) Tj
T*
(   vertical\),) Tj
T*
(   moment sense \(+CCW\), and mark all critical spans, lever arms, and inclination angles.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the analytical expressions for the resultant magnitude and direction of two concurrent forces P and Q acting at an angle theta using the Parallelogram Law.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Geometry and Vector Definition:) Tj
T*
(   Consider two concurrent coplanar forces P and Q acting at point O, with an included angle) Tj
T*
(   theta.) Tj
T*
(   Let vector OA represent force P along the horizontal axis, and vector OB represent force Q) Tj
T*
(   inclined at angle theta to OA. Complete parallelogram OACB where diagonal OC represents) Tj
T*
(   the resultant force vector R \(OC = OA + OB\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Geometric Construction:) Tj
T*
(   From vertex C, drop a perpendicular CD meeting the extension of line OA at point D.) Tj
T*
(   In right-angled triangle BCD \(or CAD\):) Tj
T*
(   AC = OB = Q, and angle CAD = angle AOB = theta.) Tj
T*
(   CD = AC * sin\(theta\) = Q * sin\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   AD = AC * cos\(theta\) = Q * cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   The total horizontal base OD is:) Tj
T*
(   OD = OA + AD = P + Q * cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of Resultant Magnitude \(R\):) Tj
T*
(   Apply the Pythagorean theorem to right-angled triangle ODC:) Tj
T*
(   OC^2 = OD^2 + CD^2) Tj
T*
(   R^2 = [P + Q * cos\(theta\)]^2 + [Q * sin\(theta\)]^2) Tj
T*
(   Expanding the algebraic terms:) Tj
T*
(   R^2 = P^2 + 2*P*Q*cos\(theta\) + Q^2 * cos^2\(theta\) + Q^2 * sin^2\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   Using the fundamental trigonometric identity sin^2\(theta\) + cos^2\(theta\) = 1:) Tj
T*
(   R^2 = P^2 + Q^2 * [cos^2\(theta\) + sin^2\(theta\)] + 2*P*Q*cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   R^2 = P^2 + Q^2 + 2*P*Q*cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   R = sqrt\( P^2 + Q^2 + 2*P*Q*cos\(theta\) \)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Derivation of Resultant Direction \(alpha\):) Tj
T*
(   Let alpha be the inclination angle of resultant R with respect to force P \(angle COD\):) Tj
T*
(   tan\(alpha\) = CD / OD = \(Q * sin\(theta\)\) / \(P + Q * cos\(theta\)\)) Tj
T*
(   alpha = atan\( \(Q * sin\(theta\)\) / \(P + Q * cos\(theta\)\) \)) Tj
T*
(   Special Cases:) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
