(   Consider two equal and opposite forces +F and -F acting at points A and B on a rigid body.) Tj
T*
(   Let 'O' be an arbitrary reference point in space. Let r_A and r_B denote the position vectors) Tj
T*
(   of points A and B with respect to origin O.) Tj
T*
(   The total moment M_O of the couple about origin O is the sum of moments of both forces:) Tj
T*
(   M_O = \(r_A x F\) + \(r_B x \(-F\)\)) Tj
T*
(   M_O = \(r_A x F\) - \(r_B x F\) = \(r_A - r_B\) x F) Tj
T*
(   Notice that vector \(r_A - r_B\) represents the relative position vector r_BA directed) Tj
T*
(   from point B to point A:) Tj
T*
(   r_BA = r_A - r_B) Tj
T*
(   Therefore, the moment simplifies to:) Tj
T*
(   M_couple = r_BA x F) Tj
T*
(   Notice that the reference origin coordinates O do not appear in this final expression!) Tj
T*
(   The moment depends solely on the relative displacement between the lines of action.) Tj
T*
(   The scalar magnitude is: |M_couple| = |r_BA| * |F| * sin\(theta\) = F * d,) Tj
T*
(   where d = |r_BA|*sin\(theta\) is the perpendicular perpendicular lever arm.) Tj
T*
(   Hence, a couple is a FREE VECTOR that can be applied at any point on the body without) Tj
T*
(   alteration.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Practical Civil Engineering Applications:) Tj
T*
(   - Torsion in bridge girders caused by eccentric vehicular lane loadings.) Tj
T*
(   - Hand-tightening of screw jacks and mechanical valves in water supply systems.) Tj
T*
(   - Wind torque on tall structural towers causing torsional twisting moments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
