BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A smooth steel sphere of weight W = 1200 N and radius r = 250 mm rests in a symmetric 90-degree V-trough whose sides are inclined at 45 degrees to the horizontal. Determine the contact forces exerted by both trough surfaces on the sphere.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Definition & Symmetry Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Weight of sphere: W = 1200 N acting vertically downwards through center O.) Tj
T*
(   V-trough geometry: Included angle = 90 degrees; left and right surfaces inclined at 45 deg to) Tj
T*
(   horizontal.) Tj
T*
(   Because the surfaces are frictionless \(smooth\), contact reaction forces R1 \(left surface\)) Tj
T*
(   and R2 \(right surface\) act perpendicular to each trough wall and pass directly through center) Tj
T*
(   O.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Angle Determinations for Forces:) Tj
T*
(   - Left surface incline = 45 deg to horizontal => Normal reaction R1 is inclined at 45 deg above) Tj
T*
(   horizontal \(pointing up and right, Quadrant I\).) Tj
T*
(   - Right surface incline = 45 deg to horizontal => Normal reaction R2 is inclined at 45 deg) Tj
T*
(   above horizontal \(pointing up and left, Quadrant II\).) Tj
T*
(   - Gravity weight W acts vertically downward \(angle = 270 deg\).) Tj
T*
(   - Angle between R1 and R2 = 90 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Angle between R1 and downward vertical W = 90 + 45 = 135 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Angle between R2 and downward vertical W = 90 + 45 = 135 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Equilibrium Equations \(Orthogonal Resolution\):) Tj
T*
(   Using Cartesian axes \(+x horizontal to right, +y vertical upward\):) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Horizontal Equilibrium \(Sigma Fx = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   R1 * cos\(45 deg\) - R2 * cos\(45 deg\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   Since cos\(45 deg\) = sin\(45 deg\) = 0.7071 => R1 = R2 = R \(Symmetric reactions\).) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Vertical Equilibrium \(Sigma Fy = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   R1 * sin\(45 deg\) + R2 * sin\(45 deg\) - W = 0) Tj
T*
(   2 * R * sin\(45 deg\) = 1200) Tj
T*
ET

