12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A cantilever beam AB of length L = 6 m is fixed at support A and free at end B. It carries a uniformly varying load \(UVL\) increasing linearly from 0 kN/m at free end B to 24 kN/m at fixed support A. Compute the support reactions at fixed end A.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Definition & Geometry:) Tj
T*
(   - Beam type: Cantilever, length L = 6.0 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Fixed support at A \(x = 0\); free end at B \(x = 6.0 m\).) Tj
T*
(   - Distributed load profile: w\(x\) = 24 * \(1 - x / 6\) kN/m.) Tj
T*
(   At x = 0 \(support A\): w = 24 kN/m.) Tj
T*
(   At x = 6 m \(free end B\): w = 0 kN/m.) Tj
T*
(   - Fixed support A provides three reactions:) Tj
T*
(   Horizontal force H_A, vertical shear force R_A, and restraint bending moment M_A.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Equivalent Concentrated Load of Triangular UVL:) Tj
T*
(   The total load W_total equals the area under the triangular loading diagram:) Tj
T*
(   W_total = \(1/2\) * base * height = \(1/2\) * 6.0 m * 24.0 kN/m = 72.0 kN.) Tj
T*
(   Centroid location of a right triangle from its vertical base \(at support A\):) Tj
T*
(   x_bar = \(1/3\) * L = \(1/3\) * 6.0 m = 2.0 m from fixed support A.) Tj
T*
(   \(Or 2/3 * 6 = 4.0 m from the apex at free end B\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Calculation of Support Reactions:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Vertical Equilibrium \(Sigma Fy = 0, Upward +\):) Tj
T*
(   R_A - W_total = 0) Tj
T*
(   R_A - 72.0 = 0 => R_A = 72.0 kN \(directed vertically upward\).) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Horizontal Equilibrium \(Sigma Fx = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   H_A = 0.0 kN \(no horizontal loads applied\).) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Moment Equilibrium about Fixed Support A \(Sigma M_A = 0, CCW +\):) Tj
T*
(   Let M_A be the counterclockwise reactive moment supplied by the wall:) Tj
T*
(   M_A - \(W_total * x_bar\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   M_A - \(72.0 kN * 2.0 m\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   M_A - 144.0 kN-m = 0 => M_A = 144.0 kN-m \(Counterclockwise\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Conclusion & Engineering Significance:) Tj
T*
(   The fixed support A must supply a vertical upward reaction of 72.0 kN and a counterclockwise) Tj
T*
(   restraining moment of 144.0 kN-m to maintain rigid equilibrium against rotation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
