/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Four concurrent coplanar forces act at origin O: F1 = 40 kN at 0 deg, F2 = 60 kN at 60 deg, F3 = 50 kN at 135 deg, and F4 = 80 kN at 240 deg. Determine the magnitude and direction of their resultant vector analytically.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Formulation & Orthogonal Components:) Tj
T*
(   To determine the resultant of concurrent coplanar forces analytically, resolve each vector) Tj
T*
(   into Cartesian rectangular components along the horizontal \(+x\) and vertical \(+y\) axes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Resolution of Constituent Forces:) Tj
T*
(   - Force F1 = 40 kN at theta1 = 0 deg:) Tj
T*
(   F1x = 40 * cos\(0 deg\) = + 40.000 kN) Tj
T*
(   F1y = 40 * sin\(0 deg\) = 0.000 kN) Tj
T*
(   - Force F2 = 60 kN at theta2 = 60 deg:) Tj
T*
(   F2x = 60 * cos\(60 deg\) = 60 * 0.5000 = + 30.000 kN) Tj
T*
(   F2y = 60 * sin\(60 deg\) = 60 * 0.8660 = + 51.962 kN) Tj
T*
(   - Force F3 = 50 kN at theta3 = 135 deg:) Tj
T*
(   F3x = 50 * cos\(135 deg\) = 50 * \(-0.7071\) = - 35.355 kN) Tj
T*
(   F3y = 50 * sin\(135 deg\) = 50 * \(+0.7071\) = + 35.355 kN) Tj
T*
ET

