(   [Problem Statement]: An overhanging beam ABC of total length 9 m is pinned at A, roller-supported at B \(x = 6 m\), with an overhang BC of 3 m. It carries a uniform load of 15 kN/m over the span AB and a point load of 30 kN at free end C. Determine all support reactions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Identification of Structural Boundary & Supports:) Tj
T*
(   - Total length: L_total = 9.0 m; Span AB = 6.0 m; Overhang BC = 3.0 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Pin support A at x = 0: Reactions R_A \(vertical\) and H_A \(horizontal\).) Tj
T*
(   - Roller support B at x = 6.0 m: Reaction R_B \(vertical\).) Tj
T*
(   - Loading details:) Tj
T*
(   * UDL w = 15 kN/m over span AB \(0 <= x <= 6 m\). Total UDL = 15 * 6 = 90 kN acting at x = 3.0 m.) Tj
T*
(   * Concentrated vertical load P = 30 kN at free end C \(x = 9.0 m\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Moment Equilibrium about Support A \(Sigma M_A = 0, CCW +\):) Tj
T*
(   - Moment due to UDL on AB: M_udl = - \(90 kN * 3.0 m\) = - 270.0 kN-m \(clockwise\).) Tj
T*
(   - Moment due to point load at C: M_C = - \(30 kN * 9.0 m\) = - 270.0 kN-m \(clockwise\).) Tj
T*
(   - Moment due to roller reaction at B: M_RB = + \(R_B * 6.0 m\) \(counterclockwise\).) Tj
T*
(   Summing moments about A:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma M_A = \(R_B * 6.0\) - 270.0 - 270.0 = 0) Tj
T*
(   6.0 * R_B = 540.0 kN-m) Tj
T*
(   R_B = 540.0 / 6.0 = 90.00 kN \(directed vertically upward\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Vertical Force Equilibrium \(Sigma Fy = 0, Upward +\):) Tj
T*
(   R_A + R_B - W_udl - P = 0) Tj
T*
(   R_A + 90.00 - 90.0 - 30.0 = 0) Tj
T*
(   R_A + 90.00 - 120.0 = 0) Tj
T*
(   R_A = 120.0 - 90.00 = 30.00 kN \(directed vertically upward\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Horizontal Equilibrium:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma Fx = 0 => H_A = 0.0 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
