(   [Problem Statement]: A 60 kg uniform circular cylinder of radius r = 300 mm is held on a smooth inclined plane of angle 30 degrees by a horizontal cable attached to its uppermost point. Calculate the tension in the cable and the normal reaction from the inclined plane \(g = 9.81 m/s^2\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. System Parameters and Gravitational Weight:) Tj
T*
(   Mass of cylinder: m = 60 kg; Weight W = m * g = 60 * 9.81 = 588.6 N acting at center O.) Tj
T*
(   Incline angle: theta = 30 degrees to the horizontal.) Tj
T*
(   Normal reaction N acts perpendicular to the incline through center O \(inclined at 60 deg to) Tj
T*
(   horizontal\).) Tj
T*
(   Cable is attached at the top of the cylinder and pulled horizontally with tension T.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Coordinate Alignment & Moment Equilibrium about Contact Point C:) Tj
T*
(   Let C be the contact point between the cylinder and the inclined plane.) Tj
T*
(   Normal reaction N passes directly through point C, so its moment about C is zero.) Tj
T*
(   Taking moments about contact point C \(Sigma M_C = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   - Component of weight down the plane: W * sin\(30 deg\) at lever arm r = 300 mm \(CCW\).) Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal cable force T has perpendicular distance to contact point C:) Tj
T*
(   Lever arm of horizontal cable about contact point C = r + r * cos\(30 deg\) = r * \(1 + cos\(30) Tj
T*
(   deg\)\).) Tj
T*
