/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A heavy circular roller of weight W = 15 kN and radius R = 600 mm is to be pulled over a rectangular curb obstacle of height h = 150 mm by a horizontal pulling force P applied at its axle center O. Calculate the minimum pulling force P required.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometry of the Roller at Impending Lift-off:) Tj
T*
(   As the roller is about to climb over the curb, contact with the ground is lost, meaning) Tj
T*
(   the ground normal reaction becomes zero: N_ground = 0.) Tj
T*
(   The entire weight is supported solely at the sharp corner of the curb \(point A\).) Tj
T*
(   Let O be the center of the roller. Drop a vertical line from O to the ground.) Tj
T*
(   Distance from O to ground = R = 600 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Height of curb = h = 150 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Vertical height of center O above curb edge A: y = R - h = 600 - 150 = 450 mm.) Tj
T*
(   In right triangle formed by center O, curb edge A, and the horizontal line through A:) Tj
T*
(   Hypotenuse OA = R = 600 mm; Vertical side = 450 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Horizontal distance from center O to curb edge A:) Tj
T*
(   x = sqrt\( R^2 - \(R - h\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 600^2 - 450^2 \) = sqrt\( 360000 - 202500 \) = sqrt\( 157500 \)) Tj
T*
(   = 396.86 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Moment Equilibrium about Curb Pivot Point A \(Sigma M_A = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   At impending motion, forces acting on the roller are:) Tj
T*
(   - Gravitational weight W = 15 kN acting downward through center O at lever arm x.) Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal pull P acting to the right through center O at lever arm y = \(R - h\) = 450 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction at corner A \(passes through A, so moment about A is zero\).) Tj
T*
(   Equating overturning moment of P to restoring moment of W:) Tj
T*
(   P * \(R - h\) = W * x) Tj
T*
(   P * 450 mm = 15 kN * 396.86 mm) Tj
T*
(   P = \(15 * 396.86\) / 450 = 5952.9 / 450 = 13.23 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The minimum horizontal force required to initiate climbing over the curb is P = 13.23 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
