/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A horizontal bracket is loaded by two forces: F1 = 100 N at angle 30 deg to horizontal at point \(2 m, 1 m\) and F2 = 150 N at angle 120 deg at point \(4 m, 3 m\). Find the equivalent force-couple system at origin \(0, 0\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Orthogonal Components of Forces:) Tj
T*
(   - Force F1 = 100 N at 30 deg:) Tj
T*
(   F1x = 100 * cos\(30 deg\) = 100 * 0.8660 = + 86.60 N) Tj
T*
(   F1y = 100 * sin\(30 deg\) = 100 * 0.5000 = + 50.00 N) Tj
T*
(   - Force F2 = 150 N at 120 deg:) Tj
T*
(   F2x = 150 * cos\(120 deg\) = 150 * \(-0.5000\) = - 75.00 N) Tj
T*
(   F2y = 150 * sin\(120 deg\) = 150 * \(+0.8660\) = + 129.90 N) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Resultant Force Vector R:) Tj
T*
(   R_x = F1x + F2x = 86.60 - 75.00 = + 11.60 N) Tj
T*
(   R_y = F1y + F2y = 50.00 + 129.90 = + 179.90 N) Tj
T*
(   Magnitude: R = sqrt\( \(11.60\)^2 + \(179.90\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 134.56 + 32364.01 \) = 180.27 N.) Tj
T*
(   Direction: theta = atan\( 179.90 / 11.60 \) = 86.31 deg above positive x-axis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Calculation of Moments about Origin O \(0, 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Using cross product M_O = \(x * F_y\) - \(y * F_x\):) Tj
T*
(   - For Force F1 at \(x1 = 2 m, y1 = 1 m\):) Tj
T*
(   M_O1 = \(2.0 * 50.00\) - \(1.0 * 86.60\) = 100.0 - 86.60 = + 13.40 N-m \(CCW\).) Tj
T*
(   - For Force F2 at \(x2 = 4 m, y2 = 3 m\):) Tj
T*
(   M_O2 = \(4.0 * 129.90\) - \(3.0 * \(-75.00\)\) = 519.60 + 225.00 = + 744.60 N-m \(CCW\).) Tj
T*
(   Total Resultant Couple at Origin:) Tj
T*
(   M_O = M_O1 + M_O2 = 13.40 + 744.60 = + 758.00 N-m \(CCW\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Final Equivalent Force-Couple at Origin:) Tj
T*
(   - Force: R = 180.27 N at 86.31 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Couple: M_O = 758.00 N-m \(Counterclockwise\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
