(   [Problem Statement]: A light cable ACB of length 5 m is fixed at support A and passes over a smooth peg B at the same level separated by 4 m. A weight W = 500 N is attached to a smooth ring C free to slide on the cable. Calculate the equilibrium position and cable tension.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometric Properties and Symmetry:) Tj
T*
(   Supports A and B are on the same horizontal level with distance L = 4.0 m.) Tj
T*
(   Total cable length: S = AC + CB = 5.0 m.) Tj
T*
(   Because ring C is smooth and frictionless, the tension in both segments AC and CB) Tj
T*
(   must be identical: T_AC = T_CB = T.) Tj
T*
(   Equal tension and horizontal equilibrium require that segments AC and CB make the same) Tj
T*
(   angle theta with the horizontal \(symmetric configuration\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Determination of Cable Sag and Angle:) Tj
T*
(   By symmetry, ring C settles at the midpoint horizontally:) Tj
T*
(   Horizontal distance from A to C = 4.0 / 2 = 2.0 m.) Tj
T*
(   Length of segment AC = 5.0 / 2 = 2.5 m.) Tj
T*
(   In right triangle formed by support A, midpoint, and ring C:) Tj
T*
