(>> Solution to Question 18:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the static determinacy and indeterminacy of beam structures, providing criteria in terms of equilibrium equations and unknown support reactions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Concepts of Static Determinacy:) Tj
T*
(   A structural system is classified as statically determinate if all external support) Tj
T*
(   reactions and internal force resultants can be uniquely determined using the laws) Tj
T*
(   of classical statics \(equilibrium equations\) alone, without considering material) Tj
T*
(   deformations or elasticity properties.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Equilibrium Equations Available for 2D Coplanar Systems:) Tj
T*
(   In a general coplanar system, there are exactly three independent equations of equilibrium:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma Fx = 0 \(Horizontal equilibrium\)) Tj
T*
(   Sigma Fy = 0 \(Vertical equilibrium\)) Tj
T*
(   Sigma M_O = 0 \(Rotational moment equilibrium about any point O\)) Tj
T*
(   Let 'r' be the number of independent unknown reaction components.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Classification Criteria:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Statically Determinate \(r = 3 and non-concurrent/non-parallel\):) Tj
T*
(   Unknowns equal equations. Examples: Simply supported beam \(pin + roller = 2 + 1 = 3\),) Tj
T*
(   Cantilever beam \(fixed support = 3 reactions\).) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Statically Indeterminate \(r > 3\):) Tj
T*
(   Equations of statics are insufficient to solve for all reactions.) Tj
T*
(   Degree of Static Indeterminacy: DSI = r - 3.) Tj
T*
(   Examples: Propped cantilever \(fixed + roller = 3 + 1 = 4 => DSI = 1\);) Tj
T*
(   Fixed-fixed beam \(fixed + fixed = 3 + 3 = 6 => DSI = 3\).) Tj
T*
(   Solution requires compatibility conditions based on beam deflection/deformation.) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Statically Unstable / Mechanism \(r < 3 or concurrent/parallel reactions\):) Tj
T*
(   The structure cannot maintain static equilibrium under general loading systems.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
