(   [Problem Statement]: A continuous frame ABC has a pin support at A and a roller support at C on a 30-degree incline. Member AB is vertical \(height 4 m\) and member BC is horizontal \(length 6 m\). A horizontal load of 20 kN acts to the right at joint B. Calculate support reactions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometry and Coordinate Setup:) Tj
T*
(   - Joint A is at \(0, 0\) with pin support \(unknown reactions H_A, R_A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Joint B is at \(0, 4 m\).) Tj
T*
(   - Joint C is at \(6 m, 4 m\) on a roller inclined at 30 deg to horizontal.) Tj
T*
(   The normal reaction R_C is inclined at \(90 - 30\) = 60 deg to horizontal \(directed up and left\).) Tj
T*
(   Components of R_C: R_Cx = - R_C * cos\(60 deg\) = - 0.5 * R_C; R_Cy = + R_C * sin\(60 deg\) = +) Tj
T*
(   0.8660 * R_C.) Tj
T*
(   - Applied load: P = 20 kN directed horizontally to the right at joint B \(0, 4 m\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Moment Equilibrium about Pin A \(Sigma M_A = 0, CCW +\):) Tj
T*
(   - Moment due to horizontal load P at B:) Tj
T*
(   M_P = - \(20 kN * 4.0 m\) = - 80.0 kN-m \(clockwise\).) Tj
T*
(   - Moment due to inclined roller reaction R_C at C \(6 m, 4 m\):) Tj
T*
(   Using Varignon's principle: M_C = \(x_C * R_Cy\) - \(y_C * R_Cx\)) Tj
T*
(   Since R_Cx pushes to the left, it creates CCW moment \(+\):) Tj
T*
(   M_C = [ 6.0 m * \(0.8660 * R_C\) ] + [ 4.0 m * \(0.5000 * R_C\) ]) Tj
T*
(   M_C = \(5.196 + 2.000\) * R_C = 7.196 * R_C.) Tj
T*
(   Equilibrium condition:) Tj
T*
(   7.196 * R_C - 80.0 = 0) Tj
T*
(   R_C = 80.0 / 7.196 = 11.12 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Calculation of Reactions at Pin A:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Horizontal Equilibrium \(Sigma Fx = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   H_A + 20 - \(11.12 * 0.5000\) = 0) Tj
T*
