(   [Problem Statement]: A bracket is attached to a vertical column by two bolts at A \(0, 200 mm\) and B \(0, -200 mm\). A vertical load of 10 kN is applied at an eccentricity of 500 mm from the column centerline. Determine the shear and tension forces on the bolts.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Equivalent Force-Couple System at Column Centerline \(0, 0\):) Tj
T*
(   The eccentric downward load P = 10 kN at x = 500 mm is equivalent to:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) A direct vertical downward shear force: V = 10 kN.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) A clockwise overturning bending couple:) Tj
T*
(   M = P * e = 10 kN * 0.500 m = 5.0 kN-m = 5000 N-m.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Bolt Shear Load Distribution:) Tj
T*
(   Assuming equal distribution among the two identical bolts:) Tj
T*
(   V_A = V_B = V / 2 = 10 kN / 2 = 5.0 kN \(shear downward on each bolt\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Bolt Normal Tension / Compression Forces due to Moment M:) Tj
T*
(   The couple M is resisted by a horizontal force couple \(T, C\) developed by bolts A and B:) Tj
T*
(   Distance between bolts: h = 200 - \(-200\) = 400 mm = 0.40 m.) Tj
T*
(   Since the moment is clockwise, top bolt A is placed in TENSION, and bottom bolt B in) Tj
T*
(   COMPRESSION:) Tj
T*
(   T * h = M) Tj
T*
(   T * 0.40 m = 5.0 kN-m) Tj
T*
(   T = 5.0 / 0.40 = 12.5 kN \(Tension on upper bolt A\).) Tj
T*
(   C = 12.5 kN \(Compression on lower bolt B\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   - Bolt A carries: Shear = 5.0 kN, Tensile load = 12.5 kN.) Tj
T*
(   - Bolt B carries: Shear = 5.0 kN, Compressive bearing load = 12.5 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 22:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and derive the condition of equilibrium for a set of coplanar non-concurrent forces using three moment equilibrium equations \(Sigma M_A = 0, Sigma M_B = 0, Sigma M_C = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Alternative Equilibrium Formulations in 2D Statics:) Tj
T*
(   The standard three equations of equilibrium for coplanar systems are:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma Fx = 0, Sigma Fy = 0, Sigma M_O = 0) Tj
T*
(   An alternative completely equivalent set of three equilibrium equations is:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma M_A = 0, Sigma M_B = 0, Sigma M_C = 0) Tj
T*
(   where A, B, and C are three distinct reference points in the plane.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Essential Constraint Condition on Points A, B, and C:) Tj
T*
(   For these three moment equations to be sufficient and completely independent,) Tj
T*
(   points A, B, and C MUST NOT BE COLLINEAR \(they must form the vertices of a non-degenerate) Tj
T*
(   triangle\).) Tj
T*
ET

