T*
(   3. Mathematical Proof of Sufficiency:) Tj
T*
(   Assume a system of forces has a resultant force R and couple moment M.) Tj
T*
(   - Condition 1: Sigma M_A = 0 requires that either R = 0 OR the line of action of resultant R) Tj
T*
(   passes directly through point A.) Tj
T*
(   - Condition 2: Sigma M_B = 0 requires that either R = 0 OR the line of action of resultant R) Tj
T*
(   passes directly through point B.) Tj
T*
(   If R != 0, conditions 1 and 2 together force the line of action of R to be the straight line) Tj
T*
(   AB.) Tj
T*
(   - Condition 3: Sigma M_C = 0 requires that the moment of R about point C must also vanish:) Tj
T*
(   R * d_C = 0) Tj
T*
(   If point C does not lie on line AB \(non-collinear\), then perpendicular distance d_C != 0.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore, the only possible mathematical solution is: R = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Since R = 0 and M_A = 0, the entire force system is in absolute static equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(   Hence, the three moment equations are proven to be fully sufficient.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
