12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A 5 m ladder AB weighing 250 N rests against a smooth vertical wall at B with its base on a smooth horizontal floor at A. A horizontal cable connects base A to the base of the wall. If a 750 N painter climbs to a distance of 3 m along the ladder from base A \(ladder inclination 60 deg\), determine cable tension and wall reaction.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometry and Coordinate Identification:) Tj
T*
(   Ladder length: L = 5.0 m; Inclination angle: theta = 60 degrees to horizontal.) Tj
T*
(   Base A is at \(0, 0\); Top B is at:) Tj
T*
(   x_B = L * cos\(60 deg\) = 5.0 * 0.500 = 2.50 m \(distance to wall\).) Tj
T*
(   y_B = L * sin\(60 deg\) = 5.0 * 0.866 = 4.33 m \(height on wall\).) Tj
T*
(   - Self-weight of ladder: W_ladder = 250 N acting at midpoint x = 2.5/2 = 1.25 m from wall, or) Tj
T*
(   1.25 m from base A.) Tj
T*
(   - Weight of painter: W_man = 750 N at distance 3.0 m along ladder from A:) Tj
T*
(   x_man = 3.0 * cos\(60 deg\) = 3.0 * 0.500 = 1.50 m from base A.) Tj
T*
(   - Smooth wall at B exerts normal horizontal reaction R_B to the left.) Tj
T*
(   - Smooth floor at A exerts normal vertical reaction N_A upward.) Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal cable exerts tension T pulling base A to the right toward the wall.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Moment Equilibrium about Base A \(Sigma M_A = 0, CCW +\):) Tj
T*
(   Clockwise moments from weights:) Tj
T*
(   M_ladder = - \(250 N * 1.25 m\) = - 312.5 N-m) Tj
T*
(   M_man = - \(750 N * 1.50 m\) = - 1125.0 N-m) Tj
T*
(   Counterclockwise moment from wall reaction R_B:) Tj
T*
(   M_RB = + \(R_B * y_B\) = + \(R_B * 4.330 m\)) Tj
T*
(   Equilibrium equation:) Tj
T*
(   4.330 * R_B - 312.5 - 1125.0 = 0) Tj
T*
(   4.330 * R_B = 1437.5 N-m) Tj
T*
(   R_B = 1437.5 / 4.330 = 332.0 N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Force Equilibrium Equations:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Horizontal Equilibrium \(Sigma Fx = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   T - R_B = 0 => T = R_B = 332.0 N.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Vertical Equilibrium \(Sigma Fy = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   N_A - W_ladder - W_man = 0) Tj
T*
(   N_A = 250 + 750 = 1000.0 N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   - Cable tension: T = 332.0 N.) Tj
T*
