(   [Problem Statement]: A crane boom OP of length 10 m and weight 6 kN \(acting at mid-length\) is hinged at O and supported by a horizontal tie cable at its top P. The boom is inclined at 50 degrees to the horizontal and carries a suspended load of 25 kN at P. Determine the tension in the cable and the pin reaction at O.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometry and Coordinate Identification:) Tj
T*
(   Boom length: L = 10.0 m, inclined at theta = 50 deg to horizontal.) Tj
T*
(   Coordinates of tip P relative to pin O:) Tj
T*
(   x_P = L * cos\(50 deg\) = 10.0 * 0.6428 = 6.428 m) Tj
T*
(   y_P = L * sin\(50 deg\) = 10.0 * 0.7660 = 7.660 m) Tj
T*
(   - Self-weight: W_boom = 6 kN acting at midpoint \(x = 3.214 m, y = 3.830 m\).) Tj
T*
(   - Suspended load: W_load = 25 kN acting downward at tip P \(x = 6.428 m\).) Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal cable attaches at P and pulls to the left with tension T.) Tj
T*
(   - Hinge at O provides reactions H_O \(horizontal\) and R_O \(vertical\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Moment Equilibrium about Hinge O \(Sigma M_O = 0, CCW +\):) Tj
T*
(   Clockwise moments \(-\):) Tj
T*
(   M_boom = - \(6 kN * 3.214 m\) = - 19.284 kN-m) Tj
T*
(   M_load = - \(25 kN * 6.428 m\) = - 160.700 kN-m) Tj
T*
(   Counterclockwise moment \(+\):) Tj
T*
(   M_T = + \(T * y_P\) = + \(T * 7.660 m\)) Tj
T*
(   Equilibrium condition:) Tj
T*
(   7.660 * T - 19.284 - 160.700 = 0) Tj
T*
(   7.660 * T = 179.984 kN-m) Tj
T*
(   T = 179.984 / 7.660 = 23.50 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Equilibrium of Forces at Pin O:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Horizontal Equilibrium \(Sigma Fx = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   H_O - T = 0 => H_O = 23.50 kN \(directed to the right\).) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Vertical Equilibrium \(Sigma Fy = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   R_O - W_boom - W_load = 0) Tj
T*
(   R_O = 6 + 25 = 31.00 kN \(directed upward\).) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Total Hinge Reaction Magnitude R_pin:) Tj
T*
(   R_pin = sqrt\( H_O^2 + R_O^2 \) = sqrt\( 23.50^2 + 31.00^2 \) = sqrt\( 552.25 + 961.00 \) =) Tj
T*
(   sqrt\(1513.25\) = 38.90 kN.) Tj
T*
(   Direction: alpha = atan\(31.00 / 23.50\) = 52.84 deg above horizontal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   Cable tension T = 23.50 kN; Pin reaction at O is 38.90 kN at 52.84 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
