(   [Problem Statement]: A system of four parallel forces of magnitudes 120 N, -80 N, 60 N, and -100 N act along vertical lines at x = 0 m, x = 2 m, x = 4 m, and x = 5 m respectively. Determine the magnitude and line of action of the resultant force.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Summation of Force Magnitudes:) Tj
T*
(   Resultant vertical force R is given by:) Tj
T*
(   R = Sigma Fy = \(+ 120\) + \(- 80\) + \(+ 60\) + \(- 100\)) Tj
T*
(   R = 120 - 80 + 60 - 100 = 0.0 N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Evaluation of Resultant Moment:) Tj
T*
