(   Since the sum of forces is identically zero \(R = 0\), the system does NOT reduce to a single) Tj
T*
(   force.) Tj
T*
(   Instead, it reduces to a pure invariant couple!) Tj
T*
(   Taking moments about origin x = 0 \(CCW positive, taking upward force as positive moment for) Tj
T*
(   positive x\):) Tj
T*
(   M_O = \(120 * 0\) + \(- 80 * 2.0\) + \(60 * 4.0\) + \(- 100 * 5.0\)) Tj
T*
(   M_O = 0 - 160 + 240 - 500 = - 420 N-m.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Verification about Another Reference Point \(x = 2 m\):) Tj
T*
(   M_2 = [ 120 * \(-2.0\) ] + [ -80 * 0 ] + [ 60 * \(4.0 - 2.0\) ] + [ -100 * \(5.0 - 2.0\) ]) Tj
T*
(   M_2 = - 240 + 0 + 120 - 300 = - 420 N-m.) Tj
T*
(   The moment is identical regardless of origin, confirming that it is a free couple.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The system has zero net linear force \(R = 0\) and reduces to a pure clockwise couple of) Tj
T*
(   magnitude 420 N-m.) Tj
