(   2. Critical Common Pitfalls to Avoid:) Tj
T*
(   - Neglecting couple moments when computing moment equilibrium about an arbitrary origin.) Tj
T*
(   - Applying the Principle of Transmissibility to evaluate internal stresses, bending moments,) Tj
T*
(   or local shear distributions \(it is valid ONLY for external rigid-body equilibrium\).) Tj
T*
(   - Using Lami's theorem when more than three forces act, or when forces are non-concurrent.) Tj
T*
(   - Misidentifying support reactions \(e.g., assigning a moment reaction to a pinned or roller) Tj
T*
(   joint\).) Tj
T*
